From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:31:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] learn_prompt: description rule names the user's words and
 triggers: frontmatter [daveey]

---
 agent/learn_prompt.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/agent/learn_prompt.py b/agent/learn_prompt.py
index feac4178b5c..526b718be4a 100644
--- a/agent/learn_prompt.py
+++ b/agent/learn_prompt.py
@@ -26,6 +26,13 @@ Frontmatter:
     Good (<=60): `Search arXiv papers by keyword, author, or ID.`
     Bad (123):   `A comprehensive skill that lets the agent search arXiv for
                   academic papers using keywords, authors, and categories.`
+  Routing is what the description is for: phrase the trigger in the user's
+  own words ("Use when <what the user says>. <behavior>." works well), not
+  in implementation terms. If the skill is easily confused with another,
+  add a `triggers:` frontmatter block instead of a longer description:
+    triggers:
+      asks: [three natural user phrasings that should load it]
+      not_for: "<near-miss task> (use <other-skill>)"
 - version: 0.1.0
 - author: always the literal value `Hermes`. NEVER fill it from the host
   environment — the OS/login username (e.g. the `user=` line in your
-- 
